{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "04",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m09p04-post-legacy-b02-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "10": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e",
        "11": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5",
        "12": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s10-c1-1f3f832be33d",
          "slide": 10,
          "text": "Choose an S3 Glacier class by how quickly you must recover an object, not just by the price of storing it. A rare read can still be urgent.",
          "text_sha256": "1f3f832be33ddeaa0f17219417b459e454347b692e1569b16383c9d1cecb947a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1f3f832be33ddeaa0f17219417b459e454347b692e1569b16383c9d1cecb947a",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s10-c2-16d13fb7d34b",
          "slide": 10,
          "text": "Glacier Instant Retrieval serves objects in milliseconds without a restore request. It still has retrieval charges and a ninety-day minimum storage duration.",
          "text_sha256": "16d13fb7d34bdd823ad5899501d298e10fc8bcb401ca55c9f65cbbe51e53b329",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "16d13fb7d34bdd823ad5899501d298e10fc8bcb401ca55c9f65cbbe51e53b329",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s10-c3-1258bd295edd",
          "slide": 10,
          "text": "Glacier Flexible Retrieval needs a restore before access. Its retrieval options trade speed for cost, and the minimum storage duration is ninety days. Deep Archive also needs a restore, generally with longer lead time and a one hundred eighty day minimum.",
          "text_sha256": "1258bd295edd8d9030cf592c4b6d173adab5e3214dc569377a6c667cad643650",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1258bd295edd8d9030cf592c4b6d173adab5e3214dc569377a6c667cad643650",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s11-c1-f6b9922e64a7",
          "slide": 11,
          "text": "Use S3 Intelligent-Tiering for changing access when you don't want to predict each object's read schedule. Distinguish the automatic instant-access tiers from the optional tiers that require a restore.",
          "text_sha256": "f6b9922e64a7a0394e5927d96bac001591eb842e14d78c483a4fa19a92f93035",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f6b9922e64a7a0394e5927d96bac001591eb842e14d78c483a4fa19a92f93035",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s11-c2-e41beec7d8d8",
          "slide": 11,
          "text": "An eligible object starts in Frequent Access. After thirty consecutive days without access it can move to Infrequent Access, then after ninety days to Archive Instant Access. Reading from these automatic tiers does not require restore.",
          "text_sha256": "e41beec7d8d8832a36d9148300af862f4ea3cd7dcccaaa7ed5609c6bb6a837c4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e41beec7d8d8832a36d9148300af862f4ea3cd7dcccaaa7ed5609c6bb6a837c4",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s11-c3-5504c46feb30",
          "slide": 11,
          "text": "The optional Archive Access and Deep Archive Access tiers have separate inactivity thresholds, at least ninety and one hundred eighty days respectively. They require a restore before reading. Don't enable them for a workload that cannot wait.",
          "text_sha256": "5504c46feb3027d2169690f119450b66a0cf6e6b5f6217e4d4635435885c7571",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5504c46feb3027d2169690f119450b66a0cf6e6b5f6217e4d4635435885c7571",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s11-c4-9bb71db354f9",
          "slide": 11,
          "text": "Objects smaller than one hundred twenty-eight kilobytes stay in Frequent Access and are not monitored for tiering. Include the monitoring and automation fee for eligible objects in the decision.",
          "text_sha256": "9bb71db354f972817becaf77323a969b374f26c48f8551ae8c3de163d2c5c5d8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9bb71db354f972817becaf77323a969b374f26c48f8551ae8c3de163d2c5c5d8",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s12-c1-cf715b260e67",
          "slide": 12,
          "text": "Plan S3 Lifecycle across the entire version history. Decide separately when to move or expire current versions, old versions, and delete markers.",
          "text_sha256": "cf715b260e67d0caee1e2e90909bc13d26b41957899e8ece08b611325ef0e60c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cf715b260e67d0caee1e2e90909bc13d26b41957899e8ece08b611325ef0e60c",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s12-c2-3a2564299599",
          "slide": 12,
          "text": "The current version can transition to a supported storage class or expire. Noncurrent versions need their own transition or expiration rule. In a versioned bucket, expiring a current object can create a delete marker without removing its older versions.",
          "text_sha256": "3a25642995990f1434c0f62fd23db82f33ff29b5de4438821338de8f99f796b4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3a25642995990f1434c0f62fd23db82f33ff29b5de4438821338de8f99f796b4",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-s12-c3-d13928e3b6ad",
          "slide": 12,
          "text": "Clean up expired delete markers only when eligible. Use a key prefix or object tag to select which objects the rule covers; a prefix isn't a folder. Check minimum duration, small-object cost, and allowed transitions before enabling the rule.",
          "text_sha256": "d13928e3b6ad880e7a7293e0ec9ea612d5bb22ad5c8e77409b7d60c5d6947c66",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d13928e3b6ad880e7a7293e0ec9ea612d5bb22ad5c8e77409b7d60c5d6947c66",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "05",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m09p05-post-legacy-b02-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "13": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322",
        "14": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830",
        "15": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s13-c1-a6d25bf3b4ea",
          "slide": 13,
          "text": "Choose the replica destination by the failure or policy boundary you need. Same-Region Replication keeps the copy in the Region, while Cross-Region Replication places it in a different Region.",
          "text_sha256": "a6d25bf3b4ea79621f168c0f83e7124fdcf83491eec9981d6618fcba80b66d2f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a6d25bf3b4ea79621f168c0f83e7124fdcf83491eec9981d6618fcba80b66d2f",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s13-c2-5278ba5e1f3f",
          "slide": 13,
          "text": "Here a versioned bucket in US East can replicate to another bucket in US East or to a bucket in US West. A separate Region can help with regional recovery or location requirements. In either design, versioning must be enabled on both buckets.",
          "text_sha256": "5278ba5e1f3f0fb3d25dd33ab0e6b5d687125331e03590ea460597360ba2fe04",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5278ba5e1f3f0fb3d25dd33ab0e6b5d687125331e03590ea460597360ba2fe04",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s13-c3-25edf5514a7c",
          "slide": 13,
          "text": "Configure the replication rule and I A M role. For objects encrypted under an AWS Key Management Service key, opt into replicating these objects and allow source key decryption and destination key encryption. Validate those permissions separately from the choice of Region.",
          "text_sha256": "25edf5514a7ce3841423abb09e4ed828f5b42fe31c7eee5f9ff95958698302fd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "92340be271362cf94cd874ae15b67c79e1481cecc192c334178063b1e80fd90e",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s14-c1-3e6069bbb1d1",
          "slide": 14,
          "text": "Treat live replication, backfill, and delete behavior as separate design choices. A live rule alone does not copy all objects that arrived earlier.",
          "text_sha256": "3e6069bbb1d123e39781e9b1bdd442d9cb6a132813f7f1c6883830f50caee089",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3e6069bbb1d123e39781e9b1bdd442d9cb6a132813f7f1c6883830f50caee089",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s14-c2-1ac7a510d78f",
          "slide": 14,
          "text": "Eligible new objects follow the live rule. Use replication metrics to watch delay and failures. S3 Replication Time Control is for more predictable live replication, not for Batch Replication.",
          "text_sha256": "1ac7a510d78f9f283c31cc29999b272a7c9424caeb492485029885eb3a436b98",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1ac7a510d78f9f283c31cc29999b272a7c9424caeb492485029885eb3a436b98",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s14-c3-652617b53f32",
          "slide": 14,
          "text": "Use S3 Batch Replication for eligible existing objects or to repair gaps. A user-created delete marker can replicate when the rule supports and enables it. Deleting a specific source version does not automatically delete the replica version.",
          "text_sha256": "652617b53f326dfc7ae642736c7a28ef5581a16fc5ea48641e55890baed00003",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "652617b53f326dfc7ae642736c7a28ef5581a16fc5ea48641e55890baed00003",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s15-c1-da6bad9bf6e2",
          "slide": 15,
          "text": "Use S3 Event Notifications to react to changes without coupling your uploader to each consumer. Plan for duplicates and events arriving out of order.",
          "text_sha256": "da6bad9bf6e2eba428fe3da6646f6f17487c1a118267c643a0c9caf31eb77b75",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "da6bad9bf6e2eba428fe3da6646f6f17487c1a118267c643a0c9caf31eb77b75",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s15-c2-a457575d325f",
          "slide": 15,
          "text": "Pick an object-created, removed, or restore event. Scope it with a literal key prefix or suffix, such as the invoices prefix or a dot C S V suffix. This is key matching, not arbitrary wildcard matching.",
          "text_sha256": "a457575d325fb78d33720136c89e2c9516190fc2f8c757eedbbe57595047c347",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "22c8fcd699e0e4e5d0990fff9af21da19be1c8c5de9a042bfef999cf860a3338",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-s15-c3-d252cd0282e6",
          "slide": 15,
          "text": "Send the event to a supported Lambda function, standard S Q S queue, or standard S N S topic and grant S3 permission to publish or invoke. Design the consumer to tolerate repeats, for example by checking a durable record of completed events before repeating an action.",
          "text_sha256": "d252cd0282e626a9c141801c8999432fcc0ee782a2739b4483e79d356619b2f2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2d8e4c63e11a426dddc1fb776c355f340ed1adfab620a64eddf92851a2e9223a",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "06",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m09p06-post-legacy-b02-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "16": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b",
        "17": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c",
        "18": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s16-c1-917afb95203d",
          "slide": 16,
          "text": "Choose EventBridge when a bucket event must reach different workflows based on its contents. The bucket sends events to the bus; rules decide which ones go to which target.",
          "text_sha256": "917afb95203dd4ccf4fcceeeaf5a05ac47643cf6e4bf723156b69781e5d113d0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "917afb95203dd4ccf4fcceeeaf5a05ac47643cf6e4bf723156b69781e5d113d0",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s16-c2-e4d8ed75c5dd",
          "slide": 16,
          "text": "Match the source, event type, bucket, and object key. In this example, the bucket is my-bucket and the key is data slash file dot C S V. A different key would not match that exact rule.",
          "text_sha256": "e4d8ed75c5dd2dcfb93a85bb555fa0aed6a34d7ee8b67aef27461f64acbedf42",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0b5d8445a83a42dc0b5c8aa039c6afc86400c849baf45233d6fa90d878af7241",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s16-c3-7b36fbce8807",
          "slide": 16,
          "text": "Send a matching event to the configured target: a Step Functions workflow, an S Q S queue, or a Lambda function. These are routing options, not three mandatory steps.",
          "text_sha256": "7b36fbce8807fca7ac5db58822f801996002cf9b28f87f9e542f8b8ac4a71be7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "341a5f50de420c3aa021a0256e660a183f791fc3d0b59d5cb45ec8b6254eeeba",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s16-c4-56294a65a837",
          "slide": 16,
          "text": "Configure target permissions. Separate retry and dead-letter handling from consumer idempotency, so a repeated delivery does not repeat the business action.",
          "text_sha256": "56294a65a837c9ddc05af64a4fa0e82ee4e1c5e87e376634085d126d72dbbbdc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "56294a65a837c9ddc05af64a4fa0e82ee4e1c5e87e376634085d126d72dbbbdc",
          "asset_sha256": "8ba94a674d400e16b6810258fa83bae4375e00b24f7cbc47c66ac2475dbe547b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s17-c1-9969acde28a9",
          "slide": 17,
          "text": "Scale high request rates across key prefixes, rather than expecting one hot prefix to handle the whole workload. The images, logs, and reports prefixes illustrate separate request patterns.",
          "text_sha256": "9969acde28a9f3810803e4839c3ec37ced1a1e759cd7e0cc1d867fd246256216",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9969acde28a9f3810803e4839c3ec37ced1a1e759cd7e0cc1d867fd246256216",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s17-c2-c891e6f3973e",
          "slide": 17,
          "text": "Prefixes are leading parts of object keys, not physical folders. S three scales partitioned prefixes as traffic grows, so these baselines are not a fixed bucket-wide limit.",
          "text_sha256": "c891e6f3973e1c9e577b0817c56c79116cdbcc0c9539b8576eef52db88956dc0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dd118ea285843ece6f6139b3d17ad2f0f27afafe0379b9d7cca16dc1f198d8a5",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s17-c3-e18bfb01841c",
          "slide": 17,
          "text": "Ramp up new traffic gradually. If you see a transient H T T P five oh three Slow Down, retry with backoff while S three adjusts to the request rate.",
          "text_sha256": "e18bfb01841cbf660df98a1b1cab27a25891a0837b33c8338c22be4479d3dd70",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a8a3dadf9491b3c54a9a06949adcf853ee535a9fb7714e364bd906cb63e27ba9",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s17-c4-0d1b3203ce67",
          "slide": 17,
          "text": "Measure the entire path. Client concurrency, network bandwidth, or A W S K M S quotas may become the limiting factor before the bucket does.",
          "text_sha256": "0d1b3203ce6786e3298a9c431717285880c7de7e9c7fda81e8a1a87ad4bd19d6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b92d91a927df20255d2913a2d1d09f6fe9b7efcbd85689f1e2a61cf6a810aab3",
          "asset_sha256": "37ca4d9c86dbd60bdf8a4ce35067098edf819dc0743a526f5298df31ede5878c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s18-c1-5a60eece400a",
          "slide": 18,
          "text": "Use multipart upload when a large transfer needs parallelism and targeted retries. Initiating it returns an upload I D, which ties the parts to one unfinished object.",
          "text_sha256": "5a60eece400aef30e56678f6fc508e91bb77653243657a8e78e9e7a5f24fd65d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dafca23f79e6828b143c513871bb7ef5f94b8749e2e5bc037309aaf15014f6a8",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s18-c2-80caefad9259",
          "slide": 18,
          "text": "Upload numbered parts in parallel. Keep the part numbers and E tags. If part two fails, resend that part without resending the others.",
          "text_sha256": "80caefad9259febde900158fe93f897b1146899ee5889fa331084823c707d0b7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "64347eec7d57587bdb9f3a39aa82502333bfad9746e51b838a3b0cf26cbeddc4",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s18-c3-e6666c33ac0b",
          "slide": 18,
          "text": "Complete the upload with the part list. Only then does S three assemble the object. For integrity, use a checksum instead of assuming the final E tag is an M D five hash.",
          "text_sha256": "e6666c33ac0b4c40b3056184aad3335ab3ee10c7ada64e044ac509838cf9f63b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9c6b2efe209f87bdc95a2fafdceeff110832dd4189904a6f580291af8ab3dd63",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p06-s18-c4-f2dac5699e21",
          "slide": 18,
          "text": "If you abandon the transfer, abort the multipart upload to remove stored parts. Consider multipart around one hundred megabytes, and use it when the object is beyond the single put limit.",
          "text_sha256": "f2dac5699e212e6bbf8e87313c6ad90fd42d5a82ecfb4a400010180df3e170be",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "872ce9001f592c597c0b32d7679d4bbfee9a2578c2b7863e7b36d7e1cc215d4a",
          "asset_sha256": "6b604e8368ae0d1f390f6eeb692f63d6a692c46722aa78c72214c59a189f6de3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "07",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m09p07-post-legacy-b02-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "19": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b",
        "20": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1",
        "21": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s19-c1-265c6048839d",
          "slide": 19,
          "text": "An interrupted upload can leave billable parts even when no completed object appears in the bucket listing. The upload I D identifies that unfinished transfer.",
          "text_sha256": "265c6048839d54a7e86d084851a90bcbd2c17ba986075d251e51ff42b944c3fd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5c268ac1796093f0155921a921a403e8937320e96410b679042e256fecf2401e",
          "asset_sha256": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s19-c2-20c55f24c990",
          "slide": 19,
          "text": "List multipart uploads to find the upload I D, then list its parts. If the transfer is still needed, upload the remaining parts and complete it; otherwise, abort it.",
          "text_sha256": "20c55f24c9901a847452a91a3c27885d3bd11db19628ec72411fcaa8eb5ae270",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0038441e8a9c691a4c0d6d040f76686b30abf851aad002640105498334c79a19",
          "asset_sha256": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s19-c3-534c06d44ab5",
          "slide": 19,
          "text": "Use an S three Lifecycle rule to abort incomplete multipart uploads after the chosen number of days. Object expiration acts on objects, not these unfinished uploads.",
          "text_sha256": "534c06d44ab5cfb232c09c52674bfc10c746588680f637d2310751fe51a3bb15",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "70935b8af913218acfc188a31aa4e803a149a0ba240496f120d090511f77cd3b",
          "asset_sha256": "fd7adcd12cb3cfffbab87e2e7044f1a3cca13d84b66826fef906b5337e6d237b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s20-c1-1039106d6986",
          "slide": 20,
          "text": "Use a byte-range get when a client needs part of an object, such as a header or media segment. Here, three requests read three separate intervals from one object.",
          "text_sha256": "1039106d69868dee08a5a5e7e0186f4d16d8b9054b5e6b6c8fb518d7062ecc78",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "10c05a4260983e57919fa72c9441fd369f6e94cdf95aa9c5b223589d50883c0b",
          "asset_sha256": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s20-c2-d824e664c310",
          "slide": 20,
          "text": "If bytes 2000 through 2999 fail, retry just that range. The client assembles the returned data in offset order, even if the requests finish at different times.",
          "text_sha256": "d824e664c310fbddd65a4959bc57bb89c8cee1622ca31f105839ee939899c0d1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d824e664c310fbddd65a4959bc57bb89c8cee1622ca31f105839ee939899c0d1",
          "asset_sha256": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s20-c3-0064847638d1",
          "slide": 20,
          "text": "Make every request read the same object revision. Pin a version I D, or use a condition such as If-Match, so the client does not assemble bytes from different versions.",
          "text_sha256": "0064847638d152d46c2f1903fcc1e66c34b4ad379be3bf305f3ef3f40b11b785",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b44e64ab986b26298f33d973e64d59bb59a8fbc5f99367190340867404acc57c",
          "asset_sha256": "6daedc0f2812e3744dcc84b3160c40cf6ccc19c8382edc718fbae46e8bc72cc1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s21-c1-8f3bef7a0bdb",
          "slide": 21,
          "text": "Try S three Transfer Acceleration when distance slows uploads. Send the request to the accelerate endpoint, enter at a nearby AWS edge, then use the AWS network to reach the bucket in its home Region.",
          "text_sha256": "8f3bef7a0bdb19b739af49cf896521115e81f37125414d395daaa92c3408a429",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e58ee44e26a9961bcb01b53ac488c98a8b719a5e0e74bb9237f551251928da1f",
          "asset_sha256": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s21-c2-692fbaad12c5",
          "slide": 21,
          "text": "Acceleration does not copy the bucket to a second Region. You can combine it with multipart upload: one improves the network path, and the other lets you transfer parts in parallel.",
          "text_sha256": "692fbaad12c5e74099342b942e0f334ce86d8f388e63fba7e6b08e44898296a9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "692fbaad12c5e74099342b942e0f334ce86d8f388e63fba7e6b08e44898296a9",
          "asset_sha256": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p07-s21-c3-0f65089549ce",
          "slide": 21,
          "text": "Compare the same workload through the regional and accelerated endpoints. Measure latency and throughput, and check whether the improvement is worth the added acceleration charges.",
          "text_sha256": "0f65089549ced95a396541407b9a3e5d0b3f9549513023a7e953e9dba71ce83f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0f65089549ced95a396541407b9a3e5d0b3f9549513023a7e953e9dba71ce83f",
          "asset_sha256": "01c2a85037c3620457b24ef837d3d711ee60df9030823a0a695b7139b3e6af69"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "08",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m09p08-post-legacy-b02-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "22": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c",
        "23": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80",
        "24": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s22-c1-c9f396bf9969",
          "slide": 22,
          "text": "S three Select is a legacy option for filtering one object. Instead of downloading the full file, a S Q L expression can ask S three to return only matching rows and selected columns.",
          "text_sha256": "c9f396bf99692efb13e95b9358de956866448af0d86e5e3f1ced863db8e1e598",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f9d3b912246c93a44cf904c5b31ccddc3bac79a4ceef643b214801ba94c97f98",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s22-c2-abdb175476cc",
          "slide": 22,
          "text": "The filter runs against one supported C S V, J SON, or Parquet object. Returning less data can reduce transfer and client processing; it is not a query across a data lake.",
          "text_sha256": "abdb175476cc90aa229582e7805e09ee021ad199d6b4d872980f33b6312fda6a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1540a52f051fb67c7c7f369b68029827cb9601b2d8b95522659625ee54d775a8",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s22-c3-b9d3311369b6",
          "slide": 22,
          "text": "S three Select is no longer offered to new customers. Existing customers can continue to use it; for a new analytics design, evaluate Athena or another suitable query engine.",
          "text_sha256": "b9d3311369b6f6e4d596e49559d8a980decd5b713bed4bc81f42e7d747d03ccf",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7e826064c4cc395f4c2b66720ac3a18810495273b3533138f397ef6817df0202",
          "asset_sha256": "ea05934cfdba43016d8da24725d470d4fa442e68813f83c389163f94d7c2827c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s23-c1-a8661cbc19d6",
          "slide": 23,
          "text": "Use Storage Class Analysis to see whether objects are read infrequently enough to move from S three Standard to Standard I A. Choose the bucket or filter the analysis by prefix or tag.",
          "text_sha256": "a8661cbc19d626eaf59d116dc760adca511698f88a0d8a342057f95dc5e468c4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b41e9df7e73167fc404dd15ad9a63c6afa74d2da34a70b64400abf535be365d7",
          "asset_sha256": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s23-c2-4c3bc14c30f1",
          "slide": 23,
          "text": "Wait for enough access history to make a decision. The first data can appear after 24 to 48 hours, but a useful recommendation commonly needs at least 30 days.",
          "text_sha256": "4c3bc14c30f1ad0850d6b834889931e43a8dd49c6faaa2a9bee62a295722b6ca",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4c3bc14c30f1ad0850d6b834889931e43a8dd49c6faaa2a9bee62a295722b6ca",
          "asset_sha256": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s23-c3-7a1325ddccb4",
          "slide": 23,
          "text": "Use the recommendation to configure a separate lifecycle rule. Analysis does not move objects and does not recommend One Zone I A or Glacier transitions. You can export the data daily as C S V for further analysis.",
          "text_sha256": "7a1325ddccb4487e9c63898fd578d23f2e7723dd18bd60939eead3e00f46eb13",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "66be7cef1a5804ae000d2047617c09e363f60f8280471b86f896c4482584a8a9",
          "asset_sha256": "9ab00bf01c070080c7da8e5163821be1d714edba2373559406e6e826ca585c80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s24-c1-07d834743312",
          "slide": 24,
          "text": "Use S three Storage Lens to spot growth, cost, and protection patterns across buckets and accounts. The dashboard rolls up metrics at different scopes, so you can narrow an organization-wide signal to a Region or bucket.",
          "text_sha256": "07d83474331267c9fa071bc943597c846a0a5605a438898b518356e092ba91f0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ff116c76af39a383294208d381490a92badb3f345db8574b9411e5d9d86bc2de",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s24-c2-ae65f213ed75",
          "slide": 24,
          "text": "Use the preconfigured default dashboard or create a dashboard with the scope you need. Prefix-level visibility is an advanced option, not something every dashboard provides.",
          "text_sha256": "ae65f213ed752d62bba527f4b37f67f8f3d4f3de3d673f78d25a6e13a236c23e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ae65f213ed752d62bba527f4b37f67f8f3d4f3de3d673f78d25a6e13a236c23e",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p08-s24-c3-8fcd54027cd0",
          "slide": 24,
          "text": "Export daily metrics as C S V or Parquet to an authorized S three destination. The dashboard identifies where to investigate; changing a lifecycle or protection policy is a separate action.",
          "text_sha256": "8fcd54027cd0e8d3ed297d50f07e977ba36dc1cc7d88532957b7711dc25fa0d3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cd5a12885f6f5ffe413fac4c91a57c468b208ca1e4b2844dba53875758adfce2",
          "asset_sha256": "5201c1e86771eb4ebed654ea9cf8f400e30d326069938f39252cc898c2169eab"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
